drm/virtio: offer ARGB8888 on the primary plane

The primary plane took XRGB8888 only, in the host's byte order, though
framebuffers may be XRGB8888 or ARGB8888.  Android's composer
(Cuttlefish's ranchu, its client target BGRA_8888) commits ARGB8888
framebuffers: the atomic check failed ("invalid pixel format AR24") and
the composer gave up presenting.  The plane now offers ARGB8888 too.

The Android kernels offer all eight 32-bit formats of the virtio-gpu
protocol.  Without blob scanouts, the host shows a resource in the format
it was created with, and dumb buffers are always created B8G8R8X8, so
only the two formats with that byte order display correctly; the alpha
channel is not used for the scanout.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@

 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_XRGB8888,
+	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_ARGB8888,
 };
 
 static const uint32_t virtio_gpu_cursor_formats[] = {
